\title{Cross-Lingual Knowledge Conflict Signals Inherit Directional Asymmetries from General Multilingual Representations}

\author{Anonymous ACL submission}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
\input{abstract}
\end{abstract}

\input{introduction}

\input{related_work}

\input{method}

\input{experiments}

\input{discussion}

\input{conclusion}

\input{limitations}

\appendix

\section{Use of AI Assistants}
\label{app:ai-assistants}

We used Claude (Anthropic) as an AI coding and writing assistant
throughout this work. Specifically:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Code:} drafting experiment scripts, data-processing
    pipelines, and analysis utilities; debugging and refactoring.
    \item \textbf{Writing:} drafting and revising paper sections,
    polishing prose, and reformatting \LaTeX{}.
    \item \textbf{Literature:} summarizing related papers to inform
    related-work section.
\end{itemize}

\section{Fine-Grained Causal Boundary Analysis}
\label{app:boundary}

Table~\ref{tab:boundary} reports steering results across the full layer gradient from an independent replication ($N = 201$, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, RTX PRO 6000).

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{Causal boundary steering results (independently sampled, $N = 201$, Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct). Bonf.\ Sig.\ $\alpha$s: number of $\alpha$ values reaching significance after Bonferroni correction out of 6 tested.}
\label{tab:boundary}
\small
\resizebox{\columnwidth}{!}{%
\begin{tabular}{lcccccc}
\toprule
Layer & Depth & Probe Acc & Best $\alpha$ & Best Fisher $p$ & Bonf.\ Sig.\ $\alpha$s & Result \\
\midrule
L12 & 38\% & 91.75\% & $+20$ & 0.085 & 0/6 & --- \\
\textbf{L13} & \textbf{41\%} & \textbf{90.00\%} & $\mathbf{+10}$ & $\mathbf{<0.001}$ & \textbf{2/6} & $\checkmark\checkmark$ \\
L14 & 44\% & 91.75\% & $+10$ & 0.002 & 1/6 & $\checkmark$ \\
L16 & 50\% & 91.50\% & $+10$ & 0.005 & 1/6 & $\checkmark$ \\
L18 & 56\% & 90.75\% & $+5$ & 0.010 & 0/6 & --- \\
L28 & 88\% & 85.25\% & $+10$ & 0.284 & 0/6 & --- \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}%
}
\end{table}

\section{Complete Steering Configuration}
\label{app:steering_config}

Table~\ref{tab:steering_config} summarizes all model--layer combinations evaluated for representation steering. Each experiment injects $\alpha \cdot \mathbf{w}_{\text{probe}}$ into the last-token residual stream, testing 3--6 values of $\alpha \in [-20, +20]$. Per-alpha breakdowns appear in Table~\ref{tab:steering}; the independent replication ($N = 201$) is in Appendix~\ref{app:boundary}.

\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\caption{All representation steering experiments. Probe Acc: EN$\to$EN balanced accuracy of the logistic regression probe at the target layer. Best $p$: minimum Fisher exact $p$-value across tested $\alpha$ values. Only Llama L13 survives Bonferroni correction. Qwen and Gemma produced zero directional flips (p$\to$c or c$\to$p) at any layer or $\alpha$.}
\label{tab:steering_config}
\small
\begin{tabular}{lcrl}
\toprule
Layer & Depth & Probe (\%) & Best $p$ \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{4}{l}{\textit{Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct ($N = 136$; 32 layers)}} \\
\textbf{L13} & \textbf{41\%} & \textbf{76.1} & $\mathbf{<0.001}$ \\
L16 & 50\% & 76.8 & 0.123 \\
L18 & 56\% & --- & 0.447 \\
L28 & 88\% & 77.6 & 0.310 \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{4}{l}{\textit{Qwen3-8B ($N = 84$; 36 layers)}} \\
L14 & 39\% & 70.2 & 0.682 \\
L18 & 50\% & 73.8 & 0.621 \\
L23 & 64\% & 73.2 & 1.000 \\
\midrule
\multicolumn{4}{l}{\textit{Gemma-2-9B-IT ($N = 158$; 42 layers)}} \\
L10 & 24\% & 70.6 & 0.214 \\
L17 & 40\% & 75.3 & 0.104 \\
L21 & 50\% & 76.3 & 0.623 \\
L24 & 57\% & 76.3 & 1.000 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\bibliography{references}

\end{document}

